  "details": "I want to have a video player send the proper file/stream to the client based on if they are on quest, pc, and maybe/eventually ios/android.\n\nI can't redirect from https to rtsp so I figured it would be better to go through yt-dlp's resolving.\n\nCurrently the User-Agent headers for everything are set to Win64\n\nThis is from quest\n\nMozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/94.0.4606.61 Safari/537.36\n\nThis is from my PC\n\nMozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/95.0.4638.17 Safari/537.36\n\nThe chrome version is technically different but that would be almost impossible to keep going\n\nI tested with AVPro but both player types go through YTDL for every case if I've got it right",
